	bipartite graph with 2n vertices, n on each side
	count perfect matchings

	brute: try all permutations

	count matchings for all subsets?

	dp[S][k] = matchings from subset S of A to elements 1..k of B
	if S is empty, exactly 1 way
	if k = 0 and S is non-empty, 0 ways
	if |S| > k, 0 ways

	dp[S][k] = dp[S][k-1] + (for all x in S with edge x-k) DP[S^x][k-1]

*/

